'''Konstantinos''' "'''Kostas'''" '''Papanikolaou''' ({{langx|el|Κωνσταντίνος "Κώστας" Παπανικολάου}}; born 31 July 1990), nicknamed "'''Air Pap'''", is a Greek professional [[basketball]] player and the [[captain (sports)|team captain]] for [[Olympiacos B.C.|Olympiacos]] of the [[Greek Basket League]] (GBL) and the [[EuroLeague]]. Standing at 2.04 [[Metre|m]] (6'8 {{1/2}}"),<ref>[http://www.euroleague.net/competition/players/showplayer?pcode=001255#!careerstats PAPANIKOLAOU, KOSTAS HEIGHT: 2.04.]</ref><ref name=Olympiacos2016>{{cite web|title=Olympiacos officially announced Papanikolaou|url=http://www.eurohoops.net/euroleague/172911/olympiacos-officially-announced-papanikolaou|work=Eurohoops.net|date=20 January 2016|access-date=20 January 2016}}</ref> he plays at the [[small forward]] position. He is widely considered among the best defensive players in European basketball.<ref name="eurohoops.net">{{Cite web |date=2018-05-08 |title=EuroLeague Best Defender by Eurohoops: Κώστας Παπανικολάου, Greeks do it better |url=https://www.eurohoops.net/el/euroleague-el-2/671268/euroleague-best-defender-by-eurohoops-kostas-papanikolaou-greeks-do-it-better/ |access-date=2022-03-18 |website=Eurohoops |language=el}}</ref>

A back-to-back EuroLeague champion with Olympiacos in [[2011–12 Euroleague|2012]] and [[2012–13 Euroleague|2013]], Papanikolaou was the [[EuroLeague Finals Top Scorer]] in [[2012 EuroLeague Final Four|2012]] and won the [[EuroLeague Rising Star]] award in [[2012–13 Euroleague#Rising Star|2013]]. He has reached another two finals with the Reds in [[2016–17 Euroleague|2017]] and [[2022–23 EuroLeague|2023]]. He is also the first player in EuroLeague history to record 2.000 points, 1.000 rebounds, 400 assists, 300 three-pointers made, 200 steals and 100 blocks.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-11-10 |title=Κώστας Παπανικολάου: Ένα απίστευτο "milestone", μοναδικό στην ιστορία της Ευρωλίγκας! (pic) |url=https://www.eurohoops.net/el/euroleague-el-2/1416925/kostas-papanikolaou-ena-apistefto-milestone-monadiko-stin-istoria-tis-evroligkas-pic/ |access-date=2023-02-07 |website=Eurohoops |language=el}}</ref> 

Since very early in his career, Papanikolaou has been a regular member of the [[Greece national basketball team|Hellenic national team]]. After winning five medals at the youth level, he helped Greece capture the bronze medal at [[EuroBasket 2025]].

